      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is super annoying and serves no purpose for VR controllers. Surely you're able to detect when a controller has lost tracking versus has disconnected completely? I still want to be able to use gestures and move around if the controller disappears behind my body. It's also super frustrating if I'm lying down and I want to perform a gesture, but instead my character has turned into one-hand-movement mode and starts running around instead! An option to disable this behaviour would be 👌",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-31T02:57:12.718Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Usually when a controller loses tracking it's not a big deal, however now when your right hand loses tracking suddenly strafing turns into turning until the controller regains tracking.\n\nThe end result is a bunch of tiny unexpected rotations for the few frames your left controller loses tracking, which can be dizzying and doesn't feel right\n\nConversely, you can no use the joystick of a controller that has lost tracking, where previously it continued to work fine even without being tracked, and you may not have even noticed your hand was out of range, now you stop being able to turn entirely.",
